From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Melser <anton.melser@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:42:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build-emscripten: add the Emscripten port and its build
 targets

Add an "emscripten" port and the build hooks the build scripts
(build-pglite.sh and pglite/ in the overlay) rely on:

- src/template/emscripten, src/include/port/emscripten.h and
  src/makefiles/Makefile.emscripten define the port: unnamed POSIX
  semaphores, poll-based waits, fdatasync as the default WAL sync
  method, no inlining, and unversioned shared libraries.
- src/backend/Makefile's pglite target links the backend the host
  embeds with POSTGRES_PGLITE_FLAGS (which carry the export list the
  build script computes from the modules it ships), as
  pgwasm/postgres.js, .wasm and .data: the glue names its wasm and its
  file package after them, and the subdirectory keeps them apart from
  the postgres target's own postgres.js and postgres.wasm.
  install-pglite installs the three into pgwasm/ of the install prefix.
  src/Makefile.shlib links shared libraries with the compiler and
  without versioned names.
- The initdb, pg_config, pg_ctl and pg_dump Makefiles install their
  .wasm outputs; pg_config and pg_ctl are wrapped by
  pglite/scripts/run_pg_cmd.mjs so other tools can run them.
- contrib/Makefile includes the overlay's contrib/dist.mk, which
  packages a contrib module as an extension archive;
  src/timezone/Makefile uses the host's zic.
- configure puts "(pgwasm-postgres $PGWASM_POSTGRES_VERSION)" into
  PG_VERSION_STR, so version() names the release.
- .gitignore ignores the build outputs.

Derived from electric-sql/postgres-pglite b133782cd759f08b3aeb263b80a963b39c7b7af1 (PostgreSQL 18.3 fork, PostgreSQL License)
